-- A fail test: this file must NOT compile. It pins where a logical operator
-- reports a non-bool operand, and that the report names that operand's type.
--
-- The blame site matters here. `or` has two forms, and the *left* operand
-- picks between them: a left operand that admits nil gets the nil-coalescing
-- default (nullable_or_default.walu, unknown_nil_coalescing.walu), everything
-- else gets the boolean form. So a boolean-form failure has to say which
-- operand does not fit and, when the right one is at fault, that the left is
-- what made the operator boolean -- otherwise the reader is sent to edit an
-- expression that could never have changed the outcome.
-- conformance: error='or' requires a bool left operand, got string
-- conformance: error=only a nullable or unknown left operand supplies a default instead
local label: string = "x"
local chosen: string = label or "y"
assert(chosen == "x")
